nodes.title:
Vapi campaigns:
- one absolute window (earliestAt/latestAt, at most 7 days ahead, one time zone);
- no recurring daily window, no per-contact retry (retry only waits up to 1 h for concurrency), no draft, read-only after launch;
- the buyer owns retries, attempt budgets and suppression.
The dashboard CSV code prepends "+" to any number (10-digit Indian mobiles become "+98..."), rejects the whole file on one empty number, and has no dedupe or opt-out column.

Vapi velocity:
- 25 weekly changelog entries with 82 items from 2026-04-13 to 2026-10-12 (about 3.3 items a week);
- October 2025 to March 2026 published only as one retroactive summary;
- SDK release gaps of 4-7 months over the same winter, then v3.0.0 of both server SDKs and the web SDK in October 2026;
- nothing India-specific shipped.

Proposed: use Vapi as the developer-surface reference for the v1 parity floor, not as an Indian-market rival. Score VP against Vapi on five runnable tasks:
- domestic Indian CLI with declared A2P;
- messy-CSV hygiene (+91 normalisation, dedupe, opt-out);
- recurring 10:00-21:00 windows with per-contact retries;
- handset reply gap on Indian PSTN;
- business-language failure reasons with a Hinglish language lock.

